{
  "case_id": "2006-06-340",
  "document_hash": "ed31cf2bb0959581d21d5d77fa814c8055e8fe048f3b2aa166a23b6590e57c42",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2006-06-340",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ed31cf2bb0959581d21d5d77fa814c8055e8fe048f3b2aa166a23b6590e57c42",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ed31cf2bb095-0000-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: We'll hear argument first today in 06-340, National Association of Home Builders versus Defenders of Wildlife, and 06-549, Environmental Protection Agency versus Defenders of Wildlife."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2006-06-340",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ed31cf2bb0959581d21d5d77fa814c8055e8fe048f3b2aa166a23b6590e57c42",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ed31cf2bb095-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Do we take the case and -- I'll ask the same question to your colleagues from the other side -- on the assumption that if the nine -- the factors in the statutes are met, that EPA has no discretion to withhold the transfer?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "National Association of Home Builders",
      "case_id": "2006-06-340",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ed31cf2bb0959581d21d5d77fa814c8055e8fe048f3b2aa166a23b6590e57c42",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ed31cf2bb095-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. KNEEDLER: Yes. That is our position, and that I think is clear from Section 402(b). It says that the administrator shall approve unless he finds that the state legal authority criteria are not satisfied."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "National Association of Home Builders",
      "case_id": "2006-06-340",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ed31cf2bb0959581d21d5d77fa814c8055e8fe048f3b2aa166a23b6590e57c42",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ed31cf2bb095-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. KNEEDLER: Our position now is that it did not have to, but -- and more fundamentally our position is that because the transfer or the approval of the State application is mandatory if these nine legal authority criteria are satisfied, EPA could not withhold approval of --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2006-06-340",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ed31cf2bb0959581d21d5d77fa814c8055e8fe048f3b2aa166a23b6590e57c42",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ed31cf2bb095-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: You mentioned a whole string of states, I think, Texas, Florida, Maine were mentioned as states that -- in connection with the transfer of the permitting authority had conditions that made the Endangered Species Act applicable."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "EPA",
      "case_id": "2006-06-340",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ed31cf2bb0959581d21d5d77fa814c8055e8fe048f3b2aa166a23b6590e57c42",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ed31cf2bb095-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. KNEEDLER: They all provided what I've described to Justice Souter, that -- that the pre-existing ESA, EPA regulations require that draft permits be furnished to the, to Fish and Wildlife and to NOAA, and that they take into account the comments by"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2006-06-340",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ed31cf2bb0959581d21d5d77fa814c8055e8fe048f3b2aa166a23b6590e57c42",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ed31cf2bb095-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: So what was done in Texas, Florida and Maine?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2006-06-340",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ed31cf2bb0959581d21d5d77fa814c8055e8fe048f3b2aa166a23b6590e57c42",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ed31cf2bb095-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: Mr. Kneedler, may I ask a question about the memorandum of agreement? That's kind of a new concept that I have a little difficulty following. Is there -- is that, is one of the nine conditions of approval that the State enter into a memorandum of agreement?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondents",
      "case_id": "2006-06-340",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ed31cf2bb0959581d21d5d77fa814c8055e8fe048f3b2aa166a23b6590e57c42",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ed31cf2bb095-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. GLITZENSTEIN: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court. I particularly start off with the memorandum of agreement that was just being discussed, and to, I think, at least try to clarify an answer, I think, to Justice Ginsburg's question about compliance with that memorandum of agreement."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondents",
      "case_id": "2006-06-340",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ed31cf2bb0959581d21d5d77fa814c8055e8fe048f3b2aa166a23b6590e57c42",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ed31cf2bb095-0001-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. GLITZENSTEIN: And it's the first full paragraph and it says: \"EPA's current practice is to consult with the Services where EPA determines that approval of a State's or a Tribe's application to administer the NPDES program may affect federally listed species.\""
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2006-06-340",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ed31cf2bb0959581d21d5d77fa814c8055e8fe048f3b2aa166a23b6590e57c42",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ed31cf2bb095-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: I don't know what you're talking about. Funding of what?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Glitzenstein",
      "case_id": "2006-06-340",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ed31cf2bb0959581d21d5d77fa814c8055e8fe048f3b2aa166a23b6590e57c42",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ed31cf2bb095-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. GLITZENSTEIN: Funding of the NPDES program carried out by Arizona that had to be approved in order to allow --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2006-06-340",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ed31cf2bb0959581d21d5d77fa814c8055e8fe048f3b2aa166a23b6590e57c42",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ed31cf2bb095-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: May I ask this question about changing position? Have you agreed and conceded that the nine statutory criteria are satisfied?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2006-06-340",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ed31cf2bb0959581d21d5d77fa814c8055e8fe048f3b2aa166a23b6590e57c42",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ed31cf2bb095-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Section 402(b) mandates that EPA approve the State's application. EPA therefore, EPA's decision therefore is not the legal cause of any effects that might happen with respect to endangered species."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2006-06-340",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ed31cf2bb0959581d21d5d77fa814c8055e8fe048f3b2aa166a23b6590e57c42",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ed31cf2bb095-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Do you mean the executive can ignore earmarks?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2006-06-340",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ed31cf2bb0959581d21d5d77fa814c8055e8fe048f3b2aa166a23b6590e57c42",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ed31cf2bb095-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: What's a mandatory decision? No, what's a discretionary decision?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2006-06-340",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ed31cf2bb0959581d21d5d77fa814c8055e8fe048f3b2aa166a23b6590e57c42",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ed31cf2bb095-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, counsel. The case is submitted."
    },
    {
